a world of 5 things, packed in rows; a life of 0 means its time is up
    row 0  0:1  life 0
    row 1  1:1  life 3
    row 2  2:1  life 0
    row 3  3:1  life 0
    row 4  4:1  life 2
the expire system walks the rows, and records a despawn for each life of 0
    record: despawn 0:1
    record: despawn 2:1
    record: despawn 3:1
the spawner makes a replacement, and gives it a life through its pending number
    record: spawn with life 1
    record: set pending 0 life 5
a second system despawns 2:1 too: it doesn't know the first one did
    record: despawn 2:1
the buffer holds 6 commands, and the world has not changed:
    row 0  0:1  life 0
    row 1  1:1  life 3
    row 2  2:1  life 0
    row 3  3:1  life 0
    row 4  4:1  life 2
apply the buffer, in the order it was recorded
    despawn 0:1: ok, 4:1 moves into 0:1's row
    despawn 2:1: ok, 3:1 moves into 2:1's row
    despawn 3:1: ok, it was the last row
    spawn with life 1: pending 0 is 3:2
    set pending 0 life 5: ok, 3:2 has life 5
    despawn 2:1: skipped, 2:1 is dead
the world after the frame
    row 0  4:1  life 2
    row 1  1:1  life 3
    row 2  3:2  life 5
